All 24 decisions recorded covering every axis A–H plus the three cross-cutting (X1/X2/X3), runner-up, and pre-mortem. Here is the full report for the synthesizer.

---

## Forcing-beat risk

The single biggest risk of productizing this is **abstraction-fitting to a sample of one**. Only two properties of the Zeinaty worked instance are actually load-bearing and validated: **blindness** (Phase 1 reconstructors see source-of-truth only) and **the orchestrator-owned runnable-test lock** (the decisive number is re-derived, never asserted). Everything else — the 3+3 redundancy count, the math/algo/protocol lens triple, the reproduce-protocol's direction-of-effect notion, and above all the *seam* — is plausible scaffolding never exercised against a second domain. If we ship a code engine with a frozen plugin interface (A1/A3/A4), the second project will need a callback we didn't anticipate, and we'll fork the engine or contort the project. Productizing the engine now pays full abstraction tax against N=1; the strongest case for X3 is that a skill protocol enforces both validated invariants at zero engine cost while deferring the unknowable seam decision until a second domain demands it.

## Winning architecture — per-axis selection table

| Axis | Chosen option(s) | One-line rationale |
|---|---|---|
| **Meta** | **X3 (engine-deferral) MERGED with the code minimum** | Ship the skill protocol; the only code is the irreducible gate + grading + anchor. Defer the engine/seam until a 2nd domain exercises it. |
| **A — seam** | **A2 fat-engine/thin-config** (parity.bth.toml args); A4 = named graduation path, A1/A3 rejected | Domain enters as natural-language TOML args, zero per-project code; maximally reversible toward A4 callbacks later. |
| **B — test authoring** | **MERGE B2 (default) + B1 (floor)** | Agent authors verbose suite from domain context; orchestrator independently re-derives the ONE decisive number (the trust boundary). B3 rejected (coverage bounded by adversary imagination). |
| **C — redundancy** | **MERGE C1 floor (3+3) + C4 severity-escalation** | Cheap breadth at validated floor, deep firepower only on DEVIATION/AMBIGUOUS clauses. C2 rejected (unjustified complexity cutoff), C3 deferred. |
| **D — Mode A/B** | **MERGE D2 channels + D3 manifest-declared + D1 delegate-to-/jax-port**; D4 deferred | "Modes" dissolve into "which evidence channels exist"; numeric channel is optional (contains /jax-port coupling); no auto-sniff of repos. |
| **E — reproduce degradation** | **MERGE E1 typed rung ladder + E3 honesty-tax**; E2 deferred | R0–R4 rungs mechanically cap the grade and keep direction-of-effect per-rung (domain-blind); substitute systems mark confound 'controlled-by-protocol'. |
| **F — gating** | **MERGE F2 conclude-gate + F3 submit-gate + F4 attest-parity/Signal 13**; F1 deferred | Submit-gate fails fast (no wasted cluster time), conclude-gate guards the Union Gate, Signal 13 is cross-project detection. Reuses existing plumbing. |
| **G — artifacts** | **MERGE G1 SHA-anchored triple + G3 docs/catalog split**; G2 deferred | Checklist/verdict/test hashed and pinned to parity_run_id; verdict → `.praxia/docs/audits/`, machine artifacts → catalog, cross-linked by run_id; drift mechanically detectable. |
| **H — ambiguity** | **MERGE H2 disagreement-signal + H1 propagating-cap**; H3 deferred | Reconstruction divergence is the domain-blind detector; load-bearing AMBIGUOUS caps grade at PARTIAL. H3 (human gate) incompatible with autonomous posture. |
| **X1 — grading** | **ACCEPT cap-lattice (min-over-ceilings)** | Grade computed from the artifact alone; absorbs E1 rung-cap and H1 ambiguity-cap as two ceilings. Core v1 code. |
| **X2 — shared library** | **DEFER (harvest-then-promote)** | Each application contributes invariant kinds; promote to shared catalog only after recurrence across ≥2 projects. This is the A2→A4 migration flywheel. |

**Coherent synthesis (one paragraph):** Ship `literature-parity` as an **X3 skill protocol** ("Validating a reimplemented baseline") whose domain surface is an **A2 `parity.bth.toml` args file** — no per-project code. The workflow runs the validated 5-phase skeleton with a **C1 3+3 floor + C4 escalation** on suspect clauses, treating Mode A/B as **D2 evidence channels** (mode **D3 manifest-declared**, numeric channel **D1 delegated to /jax-port**, optional). Ambiguity is detected by **H2 reconstruction-disagreement** and propagated with a **H1 PARTIAL cap**; reproduction fidelity is a required **E1 typed rung** with **E3 honesty-tax** status. Test authoring is **B2 agent-writes / orchestrator-re-derives** over a **B1 orchestrator-authored floor** for the decisive finding. The grade is **X1 computed by cap-lattice**, never adjudicated. Durable output is a **G1 SHA-anchored triple** placed per **G3** (verdict → audits/, machine artifacts → catalog). Enforcement is **F2 conclude-gate + F3 submit-gate + F4 attest-parity/Signal 13**. The only code built in v1: the X1 cap-lattice, the F2/F3 gate wiring, the G1 SHA-anchor, and the parity.bth.toml schema — everything else is skill protocol. A4 callbacks, X2 shared library, F1 subcommand family, and the D4/E2/G2/H3 rigor modes are named graduation paths, not v1.

## Runner-up + steelman + why-winner-wins

**Runner-up:** pure X3 skill-only MVP — a documented protocol plus parity.bth.toml schema and the F2 conclude-gate, with **no X1 cap-lattice and no submit-gate code**.

**Steelman:** It ships in days at near-zero engine cost, enforces the only two N=1-validated invariants (blindness + lock) by protocol, and defers *every* seam/parameter/grading decision until a second domain demands it — the textbook-correct way to avoid premature abstraction from N=1. Every line of code we *don't* write is a line we can't fossilize wrong.

**Why the winner still wins (no flip):** A skill section with no mechanical gate cannot make the confound legible to the Union Gate. Constraint 7 — reference_parity cannot be marked `controlled` without a passing `parity_run_id` — is a **code invariant, not a prose one**. A human-followed checklist can be silently skipped, which is the exact laundering failure mode the workflow exists to prevent. The winner is X3's *discipline and engine-deferral* PLUS the irreducible code minimum (X1 + F2/F3 + G1) that makes the verdict machine-enforced rather than honor-system. I accept X3's deferral of the engine; I reject X3's "pure prose, zero code" reading. The flip does not happen.

## Pre-mortem (failed 6 months out)

1. **Engine fossilization** — we built A1/A3 anyway; the second project needed a callback we lacked; the team forked the engine. *Pre-empted by:* A2 thin-config seam + A4 as a *named* graduation path — there is no frozen interface to fossilize.
2. **Gate theater** — the skill shipped but the parity step stayed advisory; confirmatory campaigns concluded with reference_parity silently uncontrolled and the workflow caught nothing. *Pre-empted by:* F3 HARD-block at submit (validation/production) + F2 conclude-gate + F4 Signal 13 — three independent enforcement points, not one checklist.
3. **Grade inflation** — graders called borderline cases PARITY to unblock campaigns, reintroducing the discretion the workflow removes. *Pre-empted by:* X1 mechanical cap-lattice (grade = min-over-ceilings from the artifact, with E1 rung-cap and H1 ambiguity-cap mandatory) + G1 SHA-anchor making a stale or tampered verdict mechanically detectable.

